KNOWNBUG
temporal_assumption1.sv

^\[main\.assume\.1\] always \(main\.a \|=> main\.b\): ASSUMED$
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.s -> main\.b: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
recurrence_diameter (src/ebmc/completeness_threshold.cpp) computes the
completeness threshold from the state variables of the design only.
Assumptions with temporal operators add hidden state (here, the value
of a in the previous cycle), which increases the recurrence diameter.
The heuristic engine reports "PROVED (CT=1)", but BMC with bound 2
finds a counterexample that satisfies the assumption.
